# Files that must never be committed
.env
.env.*
*.before-install

# Editor and OS leftovers
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Logs and temporary files.
# The leading slash matters on both folder names. A bare `logs/` matches a folder
# of that name at ANY depth, which was quietly hiding the admin Activity Log
# screen (dashboard/admin/logs.php) from the repository - it rendered on the live
# site but a fresh clone had no such page. Only a logs/ or tmp/ folder at the
# root of the project is scratch.
/logs/
/tmp/
*.log

# Uploads and anything a person drops in by hand. The folders and their
# .htaccess files are kept, so a fresh clone still has somewhere to write and
# still has the script protection. The `**` matters: `/uploads/*` would only
# match one level down, which lets a picture in uploads/events/ slip through.
/uploads/**
!/uploads/
!/uploads/.htaccess
!/uploads/*/
!/uploads/*/.htaccess

# The same thing again for where the uploads actually live. UPLOAD_FOLDER in
# app/config.php points at assets/uploads, not at the root of the site, so the
# block above was ignoring a folder that does not exist and every photograph
# somebody uploaded was about to be committed.
/assets/uploads/**
!/assets/uploads/
!/assets/uploads/.htaccess
!/assets/uploads/*/
!/assets/uploads/*/.htaccess

# Scratch files somebody was using to compare rendered pages. They are saved
# page dumps and one-off test scripts, kept out of the repository so the
# webroot stays clean. Delete them whenever you like - the site does not use
# them.
/test.php
/*.html
/*.jar
/*.orig-backup

# vendor/ is deliberately NOT ignored. There is no build step on this site:
# the server runs the PHP exactly as it is committed, so the libraries have to
# be in the repository for a fresh clone to work. Run `composer install` to put
# them back if you ever delete this folder.
AGENTS.md
